From: Hans Christian Winther-Sorensen <hc@wsh.no>
Subject: [PATCH] sparc32: give the SS-5's CS4231 "intr" 9, the processor level
 of its SBus level

The SUNW,CS4231 node had "interrupts" 5 and "intr" 5. "interrupts" is the
SBus level and "intr" the processor level, and on sun4m SBus level 5 is
processor level 9: the two said different things. Solaris takes
"interrupts" and waits at level 9, SunOS 4 takes "intr" and waits at
level 5, so no interrupt line served both. The SS-5's own PROM (2.15)
gives the chip "intr" 0x39: an SBus interrupt at processor level 9.

Make "intr" 9, so both systems wait where the chip interrupts (with the
QEMU change that raises the SS-5's cs4231 at SBus level 5, as on the real
machine).
---
 drivers/sbus.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/sbus.c b/drivers/sbus.c
index d59963e..475cb15 100644
--- a/drivers/sbus.c
+++ b/drivers/sbus.c
@@ -213,7 +213,11 @@ ob_cs4231_init(unsigned int slot)
     push_str("reg");
     fword("property");
 
-    PUSH(5);
+    /*
+     * SBus level 5 ("interrupts" below) is processor level 9 on sun4m, as
+     * the SS-5's own PROM has it: "intr" is the processor level.
+     */
+    PUSH(9);
     fword("encode-int");
     PUSH(0);
     fword("encode-int");
